WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Hello, today we are going to talk about a

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.000
tool that simplifies something we

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
do every day: payments. In an

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
increasingly digital world, we will see

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.000
how a solution that is likely already

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.000
on many phones is changing

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.000
small daily transactions.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.000
I'm sure this situation sounds familiar

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.000
to everyone, right? Having to look for that

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
very long account number for a friend

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.000
or rummaging through your pockets to

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
find the exact change for a coffee.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.000
A common daily hassle that

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
we know all too well. Well, the solution

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.000
is actually much simpler than it

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.000
seems. It's about moving from the

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.000
complexity of IBAN numbers to the

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.000
simplicity of something we use all the

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.000
time: a phone number. Okay, let's

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.000
get to it. The tool that

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
achieves this is Bizum. And the most

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.000
interesting part is that most likely

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.000
it's already integrated into most

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.000
phones, sometimes without us even

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
noticing. So, what is it

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
exactly? Well, it's very easy. Bizum is

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000
a free service found inside our

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.000
bank's application. Its

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
main function is to let us send

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.000
and receive money instantly between

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.000
individuals using just a phone

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.000
number, nothing else. And its advantages

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.000
are very clear. First, it's free. Second,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
and this is key, it's already in the

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.000
bank's app. What does this mean? It

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.000
means you don't have to download anything new,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.000
create extra accounts, or learn to

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.000
use a new app from scratch. It's already

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.000
there. Now let's move to one of its greatest

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.000
virtues: speed. We aren't just talking about

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.000
fast payments, we are talking about payments

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000
that are practically instant. Look

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.000
at this fact: Less than 5 seconds. That

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.000
is how long it takes for money to

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.000
travel from one bank account to another.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.000
In fact, it's almost faster than taking

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.000
 your wallet out of your pocket. This

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.000
makes it perfect for daily

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.000
situations. No more running out of

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.000
change for a coffee or struggling to

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.000
collect money for a group gift.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Now everything is solved with a couple

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.000
of taps on the screen. Great, we've

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
seen what it is and why it's so

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.000
useful. Now for the big question:

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.000
How do you use it? Let's see it step by step,

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.000
as it's very, very simple. Before

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.000
starting, there's only one requirement: having a

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.000
mobile phone with your bank's app

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.000
installed. And that's it, nothing

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.000
else. The process is straightforward. First,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.000
open your usual bank app.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Second, look for the Bizum or

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.000
send money section. Third,

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.000
choose a contact directly from your

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.000
address book. And fourth, enter the

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.000
amount and confirm the operation,

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.000
usually with the same password you

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.000
use for other transactions. Just

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.000
like that. And we reach a fundamental

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.000
point, one that is sure to

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.000
raise questions. When we talk about

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.000
money, security comes first. So,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.000
is it safe to use this service? It's a

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.000
direct question, right? Can we

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.000
trust this system? Well, the

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.000
answer is a resounding yes. And the key

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.000
is this: Bizum has the guarantee and

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.000
security of the bank itself. Note that

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.000
it's not an external app, it's a

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.000
service that operates with the same

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.000
security systems as any other

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.000
bank transfer you already make.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.000
In the end, it's about being able to

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.000
manage daily payments in a

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.000
convenient, fast and, above all,

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.000
secure way. It's a tool designed for

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.000
current times and to make our

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.000
financial lives a little easier. And

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.000
to finish, we leave you with a final thought.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.000
With all this in mind, how about

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.000
trying it sometime? You might

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.000
discover a much simpler way to

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.000
manage your day-to-day money.
